					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctornovakaine" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3003380); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3003380&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605861464" alt="DoctorNovakaine" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3003380)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctornovakaine" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3003380); return false;" >DoctorNovakaine</a></span> <span class="odate time_1534962009 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Aug 2018 18:20</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3922008">
									

<p>I wish I felt intrigue rather than confusion. I like a good &quot;unexplained mysteries&quot; vibe, I would spend hours some nights looking at some of the most mysterious unsolved cases the world has to offer back in the day. This is clearly building off of that foundation, and it starts off so promising.</p>
<p>But it never capitalizes on it. It never gives that thing that I can sink my teeth into, that one aspect that weaves the bits into that captivating net that catches my intrigue. We get these journals that are supposed to tell a story but end up too disjointed to truly follow, and even if we could they might be utterly meaningless. Part of it might be that the researchers never really connect, I didn't really get invested in them, certainly not the writer. It seems clear that the video footage is supposed to be the payoff, but I don't really get anything from it, either because the build-up didn't clearly lead towards it or because again we're lead to feel like it's potentially unreliable. The whole &quot;maybe it didn't happen at all&quot; thing sort of kills the intrigue, because then we don't even really know what the story is.</p>
<p>It is a shame, because the fuel is there. This has the potential to reach that &quot;unsolved mysteries&quot; vibe. It just isn't there right now.</p>

							</div>

								
					
