														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3974205">
									

<p>I liked it, actually. I admit that it did take me a second, and I got the first inklings of an idea of what might be going on, and you just built on it over time.<br />
My take away was this, and I think the writer was trying to clue us in, as well; the wire was falling into a &quot;void,&quot; as they put it. The lack of existence is what lies on the other side of the door. It seems as though anything that passes through is erased from the memories of everyone left alive. All of the redundant documents and repeated requests have been fulfilled and carried out, but every test completed would wipe your memory of completing the test.<br />
The only pill I find hard to swallow is the idea that the Foundation wouldn't have caught on, though. I doubt they'd let things go this badly for such an extended period of time before realizing that something wasn't quite right.</p>

